ODS-OS coreutils POSIX Compliance Statement
============================================

This document lists the exact standard headers and system calls used by each
tool in ods-coreutils. All tools target POSIX.1-2008 (IEEE Std 1003.1-2008)
with XSI extensions, and are built with:

  -D_POSIX_C_SOURCE=200809L -D_XOPEN_SOURCE=700

Global headers used across multiple tools:
  <stdio.h>, <stdlib.h>, <string.h>

Tier 1 — trivial, no filesystem writes
---------------------------------------

echo (src/echo.c)
  Headers: <stdio.h>
  Syscalls: none

pwd (src/pwd.c)
  Headers: <stdio.h>, <unistd.h>
  Syscalls: getcwd()

cat (src/cat.c)
  Headers: <stdio.h>, <stdlib.h>
  Syscalls: none (uses stdio fopen/fread/fwrite/fclose)

Tier 2 — basic filesystem read
-------------------------------

head (src/head.c)
  Headers: <stdio.h>, <stdlib.h>, <string.h>
  Syscalls: none (uses stdio)

tail (src/tail.c)
  Headers: <stdio.h>, <stdlib.h>, <string.h>
  Syscalls: none (uses stdio fseek/ftell)

ls (src/ls.c)
  Headers: <stdio.h>, <stdlib.h>, <string.h>, <dirent.h>, <sys/stat.h>,
           <pwd.h>, <grp.h>, <time.h>
  Syscalls: none (uses opendir/readdir/closedir, stat)

du (src/du.c)
  Headers: <stdio.h>, <stdlib.h>, <string.h>, <dirent.h>, <sys/stat.h>, <unistd.h>
  Syscalls: lstat()

df (src/df.c)
  Headers: <stdio.h>, <stdlib.h>, <string.h>, <sys/statvfs.h>
  Syscalls: statvfs()

Tier 3 — filesystem writes / structure
---------------------------------------

mkdir (src/mkdir.c)
  Headers: <stdio.h>, <stdlib.h>, <string.h>, <sys/stat.h>, <errno.h>
  Syscalls: mkdir()

rmdir (src/rmdir.c)
  Headers: <stdio.h>, <unistd.h>
  Syscalls: rmdir()

touch (src/touch.c)
  Headers: <stdio.h>, <stdlib.h>, <string.h>, <sys/stat.h>, <fcntl.h>,
           <unistd.h>, <utime.h>, <time.h>
  Syscalls: stat(), open(), close(), utime()

cp (src/cp.c)
  Headers: <stdio.h>, <stdlib.h>, <string.h>, <sys/stat.h>, <fcntl.h>,
           <unistd.h>, <dirent.h>, <errno.h>
  Syscalls: open(), read(), write(), close(), stat(), mkdir(),
            opendir(), readdir(), closedir()

mv (src/mv.c)
  Headers: <stdio.h>, <stdlib.h>, <string.h>, <sys/stat.h>, <fcntl.h>, <unistd.h>, <errno.h>
  Syscalls: rename(), stat(), open(), read(), write(), close(), unlink()

rm (src/rm.c)
  Headers: <stdio.h>, <stdlib.h>, <string.h>, <sys/stat.h>, <unistd.h>,
           <dirent.h>, <errno.h>
  Syscalls: lstat(), unlink(), rmdir(), opendir(), readdir(), closedir()

chmod (src/chmod.c)
  Headers: <stdio.h>, <stdlib.h>, <string.h>, <sys/stat.h>
  Syscalls: chmod(), stat()

chown (src/chown.c)
  Headers: <stdio.h>, <stdlib.h>, <string.h>, <pwd.h>, <grp.h>, <unistd.h>
  Syscalls: chown()

Tier 4 — search / text processing
-----------------------------------

grep (src/grep.c)
  Headers: <stdio.h>, <stdlib.h>, <string.h>, <regex.h>, <dirent.h>, <sys/stat.h>
  Syscalls: none (uses regcomp/regexec from POSIX regex library)

find (src/find.c)
  Headers: <stdio.h>, <stdlib.h>, <string.h>, <ftw.h>, <sys/stat.h>
  Syscalls: nftw()

tree (src/tree.c)
  Headers: <stdio.h>, <stdlib.h>, <string.h>, <dirent.h>, <sys/stat.h>
  Syscalls: none (uses opendir/readdir/closedir, stat, scandir)

Tier 5 — process monitoring / control
---------------------------------------

ps (src/ps.c)
  Headers: <stdio.h>, <stdlib.h>, <string.h>, <dirent.h>, <unistd.h>
  Syscalls: none (reads /proc filesystem via opendir/readdir/fopen/fgets)

top (src/top.c)
  Headers: <stdio.h>, <stdlib.h>, <string.h>, <dirent.h>, <unistd.h>,
           <termios.h>, <sys/select.h>, <sys/ioctl.h>, <time.h>
  Syscalls: tcgetattr(), tcsetattr(), nanosleep(), select(), read(),
            ioctl()

kill (src/kill.c)
  Headers: <stdio.h>, <stdlib.h>, <string.h>, <signal.h>, <strings.h>, <unistd.h>
  Syscalls: kill()

Tier 6 — editor / pager
------------------------

less (src/less.c)
  Headers: <stdio.h>, <stdlib.h>, <string.h>, <regex.h>, <termios.h>,
           <unistd.h>, <sys/ioctl.h>, <sys/select.h>
  Syscalls: tcgetattr(), tcsetattr(), read(), ioctl(), select(),
            regcomp/regexec()

nano (src/nano.c)
  Headers: <stdio.h>, <stdlib.h>, <string.h>, <termios.h>, <unistd.h>,
           <sys/ioctl.h>, <sys/select.h>
  Syscalls: tcgetattr(), tcsetattr(), read(), ioctl()
